-- title:
--   Sign-flip transport of the local GL₃ package, gauge edition
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\psi_v$ be the standard additive character `psiLocal` of the completion $\mathbb{Q}_v$; write $q=\mathrm{absNorm}(v)$ and $G=\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$. Let $W:G\to\mathbb{C}$ satisfy $W(u(x,y,z)g)=\psi_v(x+y)W(g)$ for all upper unipotent $u(x,y,z)$, $W(1)=1$, Whittaker multiplicity one for the cyclic representation generated by $W$ (the Whittaker functional space of `gl3CyclicRep` has rank $\le 1$), the irreducibility condition that every nonzero $F$ in the span of right translates of $W$ has $W$ in the span of its own right translates, smoothness (some open subgroup fixes $W$ on the right) and admissibility (for every open subgroup $U_v$, the $U_v$-fixed vectors of the cyclic space lie in the span of a finite set). Assume a two-parameter gauge majorant: constants $B$, $t\in\mathbb{N}$, $C$ such that $W(h)=0$ unless both $|\det h|\,\sigma_{\mathrm{row}}(h)/\sigma_{\mathrm{minor}}(h)^2\le B$ and $\sigma_{\mathrm{minor}}(h)/\sigma_{\mathrm{row}}(h)^2\le B$, and in that range $\|W(h)\|\le C$ divided by the $t$-th power of the product of these two quantities, where $\sigma_{\mathrm{row}}$, $\sigma_{\mathrm{minor}}$ are the sup-norms of the last row and of the bottom $2\times2$ minors. Assume a unitary central character: a homomorphism $\omega_v:\mathbb{Q}_v^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$ of absolute value $1$ with $W(\mathrm{diag}(t,t,t)h)=\omega_v(t)W(h)$. Let $\varpi$ be an element of the valuation ring with nonzero image of valuation $\exp(-1)$, let $E,E^\vee$ be complex polynomials, $\varepsilon\ne0$, $\ell\in\mathbb{N}$, and assume for every $g\in G$ a $\mathrm{GL}_3\times\mathrm{GL}_1$ functional-equation package: there are $P:\mathbb{C}\to\mathbb{C}$ and $\sigma_0,\sigma_1\in\mathbb{R}$ with $P$ rational in $q^{-s}$ up to a power $q^{ms}$ (i.e. $P(s)R(q^{-s})=Q(q^{-s})q^{ms}$ for polynomials $Q,R$, $R\ne0$), the integral `localZeta30` for $W$ with trivial character convergent for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_0$ and equal to $E(q^{-s})^{-1}P(s)$ there, the integral `localZeta31` for `dualWhittakerFn3 W` at $w'\,{}^t g^{-1}$ convergent for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_1$, and $\mathrm{localZetaDual31}(1-s,g)=E^\vee(q^{-(1-s)})^{-1}\bigl(\varepsilon q^{\ell(1/2-s)}\bigr)P(s)$ for $\mathrm{Re}(1-s)>\sigma_1$; the measures are the multiplicative Haar measure obtained by pulling back `mulMeasure (selfDualHaarAt ℚ v)` along $\mathbb{Q}_v^\times\to\mathbb{Q}_v$ and the self-dual additive measure. Then there exist $W_0:G\to\mathbb{C}$ and $d\in G$ such that $W_0$ is a local Whittaker datum for $\psi_v^{-1}$ (all six conditions above, with $\psi_v$ replaced by $\psi_v^{-1}$), $W_0$ has central character $\omega_v$, $W_0$ admits a gauge majorant of the same shape for some constants, and there is $\varepsilon_0\ne0$ with $\varepsilon_0^2=\varepsilon^2$ for which $W_0$ satisfies, at every $g$, the same functional-equation package with the same $E$, $E^\vee$, $\ell$ and with $\varepsilon_0$ in place of $\varepsilon$; moreover $F\mapsto F(d\cdot d^{-1})$ carries the cyclic space of $W_0$ into that of $W$ and $F\mapsto F(d^{-1}\cdot d)$ carries that of $W$ into that of $W_0$, $d$ commutes with all torus points `iotaTorusLocal v n` and `twoRowPointLocal v k₁ k₂`, conjugation by $d$ preserves each set `congruenceK1 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v c`, $W_0(g)=W(dgd^{-1})$ for all $g$, $d$ is the image under `iotaGL` of $(-1)\cdot\mathrm{diag}(-1,1)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2$, and $d$ lies in `congruenceK1 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v c` for every $c$.
--
--   This is the sign-flip transport of the local package attached to a place $v$ in the cubic-induction argument: conjugation by the diagonal sign matrix $\mathrm{diag}(1,-1,1)$ negates both simple-root coordinates of the unipotent radical, hence turns a $\psi_v$-Whittaker function into a $\psi_v^{-1}$-Whittaker function while preserving $|\det|$ and the sup-norms of the last row and of the bottom $2\times2$ minors, so the gauge majorant, the central character and the local functional equations survive with the epsilon factor changed only up to sign. It is used in the construction of Whittaker vectors lying in the congruence subgroups $K_1(\mathfrak{p}^c)$ and in the conductor-bounded level statement for ramified places.
